<title>NETHERLANDS: Akzo unit to set up R&amp;D facility.</title>
<headline>Akzo unit to set up R&amp;D facility.</headline>
<dateline>ARNHEM, Netherlands 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chemical group Akzo Nobel NV said on Tuesday its Intervet veterinary products subsidiary planned to invest some 30 million guilders in a new research and development facility in Angers, France.</p>
<p>It said the investment was in line with Intervet's strategy to step up its global presence on the veterinary products market.</p>
<p>Intervet said its existing pharmaceuticals research and development facility in Boxmeer, Netherlands, would be relocated to France.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
